# Welcome to WCHNT

This is the live editor for **WCHNT — We CAN Have Nice Things**, an experimental
object-oriented language. Everything here runs in your browser.

## What you're looking at

The editor holds a `.wcn` file: ordinary markdown whose code lives in fenced blocks under a
few headings — `## Schema`, `## Construction`, `## Methods`, and `## Target`.

- **Run** builds the program. Canvas games play in the window; **[[adventure]]**
  uses a text transcript. **Close** stops it; the next Run rebuilds from Construction.
- **Go** opens an existing page by name; **New** creates a sibling page. Link pages with `[[PageName]]`.
- Pages are saved in your browser (localStorage), so they survive reloads.

## Try it

- **[[bounce]]** — the classic bouncing ball from the tutorial.
- **[[shapes]]** — a circle, square, and triangle drifting across the screen.
- **[[square]]** — click the play area, then steer with the arrow keys.
- **[[pollution]]** — a little arcade game. Click the canvas after Run, then steer with the
  arrow keys.
- **[[adventure]]** — a ten-room text world. Type `N` `E` `S` `W` and press Enter.
- **[[writepaths]]** — a six-level world. Type `jets`, `ocean`, `resize`, or a fountain name.
- **[[flyingA]]** — a shape box that publishes `Shape`, `make`, `addShape`, and `update!`.
- **[[flyingB]]** — imports flyingA and adds a `Pentagon`. Run this page to see the membrane.
- **[[factory_args]]** — Target builds a `Pen` and passes it into `SketchAssemblage.factory(pen)`.
- **[[combinators]]** — `map` / `filter` / `fold` on arrays and maps. Press Enter; `println` formats the values.
- **[[maths]]** — `wchntMaths` injected via `@`. Press Enter to pull three `randInt`s.
- **[[origin]]** — Patternflow concentric tiles. Move the mouse; hold Shift for mode/freq.

## Learn more

The language itself is documented on the [WCHNT website](https://synaesmedia.net/apps/wchnt/).
If you just want to jump in, edit the Schema and Construction and hit Run — most things you
change will show up immediately.
